---
import Guide from "@layouts/Guide.astro";
import Alert from "@components/Alert.astro";
import StatusTag from "@components/StatusTag.astro";
import DocScanScreen from "@components/phone/DocScanScreen.astro";
import LivenessScreen from "@components/phone/LivenessScreen.astro";
import { WALLET_NAV } from "@data/nav-sections";

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", href: "/" },
  { name: "Wallet", href: "/wallet" },
  { name: "Mobile wallet", href: "/wallet/mobile-wallet" },
];
---

<Guide
  title="Mobile wallet"
  metaTitle="Mobile wallet — capture and verify | identity.org.au"
  description="The mobile wallet is where verification happens: guided document capture, selfie with active liveness, biometric hardware capture, device integrity attestation, and on-device encryption before anything moves."
  lede="The capture side of the Identity Wallet: your phone's camera, sensors and secure hardware do the verification work — and encrypt everything before it leaves your hands."
  eyebrow="The service"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
  sectionLabel="The wallet"
  sectionNav={WALLET_NAV}
>
  <StatusTag tone="info">Open-source reference implementation</StatusTag>

  <div class="prose-service mt-6">
    <p>
      Verification evidence can only be produced where the person and the device meet — so the
      mobile wallet is where your identity is actually verified. It is a guided capture app: it
      walks you through each evidence step, checks quality as you go, lets you review everything,
      and encrypts the whole payload on your phone before a single byte is transmitted.
    </p>

    <h2>The capture pipeline</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Guided document capture.</strong> Front and back of your identity document, framed
        with on-screen corner guides. The app checks edges, focus and glare in real time, and the
        document's text is read by OCR so you can correct any misread field before submission.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Selfie with active liveness.</strong> Short challenges — blink, turn your head,
        smile — issued unpredictably and verified live. A photo, replayed video or rendered face
        cannot answer a challenge it has not seen; this is the core defence against
        <a href="/insights/deepfakes-and-identity-verification">deepfake and replay attacks</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Biometric hardware capture.</strong> For the
        <a href="/get-started/verification-levels">Trusted level</a>, fingerprint or iris capture
        runs through your phone's platform-secure APIs — inside secure hardware the operating
        system cannot read into — with liveness and anti-spoofing signals.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Device integrity attestation.</strong> Google Play Integrity on Android and Apple
        App Attest on iOS let your device prove the app is genuine and the system untampered,
        closing off the emulators and injection tools that industrial fraud relies on.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>On-device encryption.</strong> Templates and payloads are encrypted on your phone
        with envelope encryption (X25519-XSalsa20-Poly1305) before transmission. The network
        receives ciphertext it can verify against but never browse.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[260px]">
      <DocScanScreen />
    </div>
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[260px]">
      <LivenessScreen />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="prose-service mt-10">
    <h2>What never leaves your phone unprotected</h2>
    <p>
      The design rule is simple: raw evidence is processed at the edge, and only encrypted
      payloads and signed results move. Your document images and biometric templates are encrypted
      before transmission; verification produces a
      <a href="/help/understanding-your-veid-score">score and tier</a> recorded on the network;
      and services that rely on your identity receive
      <a href="/help/who-can-see-your-data">answers, never evidence</a>. The full model — keys,
      revocation, deletion — is on the <a href="/wallet/security">wallet security</a> page.
    </p>

    <h2>After capture: the wallet role</h2>
    <p>
      Once verified, the mobile app is also a wallet: your credential card, your shareable proofs
      and your consent activity live on the device, and requests from services appear there for
      approval. The same identity is available in the browser at
      <a href="/wallet/web-wallet">my.identity.org.au</a> — capture is mobile-only, management is
      everywhere.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Alert tone="warning" title="No app-store listings" class="mt-8">
    <p>
      The mobile wallet is an open-source <strong>reference implementation</strong> — the working
      blueprint production wallets build on, published in the
      <a href="/about/open-source" class="link-plain">VirtEngine repository</a>. There are no
      official app-store listings at this stage. Treat any store listing claiming to be this
      wallet as suspect and <a href="/help/recognising-scams-and-phishing" class="link-plain">report it</a>.
    </p>
  </Alert>
</Guide>
